# The smart-serial console's link, in trouble (shared/sscon.c, the sserial
# component, shared/comps/term.c):
# - a line longer than the console's 63 characters is dropped, the next
#   one works;
# - the link goes away in the middle of a long reply (LinuxCNC stopped):
#   the drive times out (sserial0.connected 0) and resets its end; LinuxCNC
#   comes back with a fresh end; the next command answers whole, with no
#   left-over bytes of the old reply;
# - console traffic while the drive is enabled and moving: no fault;
# - a command typed on USB answers on USB and is copied to the console.
@args --drive ../hwtest/burnin/ECMA-C30604FS/stmbl.conf
@timeout 120
lcnc 0 0
run 0.5
con about
run 0.5
conread
con fault0.state = 0 # this line is far too long for the drive's console buffer of sixty-four bytes
run 0.5
con pe0.idle
run 0.5
conread
con showconf
run 0.3
lcncstop
run 0.2
sserial0.connected
conreset
lcnc 0 0
run 0.2
sserial0.connected
conread
con about
run 0.5
conread
lcnc 1 0
run 0.5
lcnc 1 31.4
con fault0.state
run 0.3
con pe0.p_in
run 0.3
con about
run 0.6
conread
fault0.state
about
run 0.5
conread
@match ^con> STMBL simulated drive
@match ^con> pe0.idle = 
@reject ^con> fault0.state = 0 # this
@expect sserial0.connected[1] == 0
@expect sserial0.connected[2] == 1
@match ^con> fault0.state = 1\.0+$
@expect fault0.state == 1
@match ^STMBL simulated drive
@reject ^con> error
